    All rights reserved. BSD 2-Clause; see Sensor.php for the full text.

    Services -> SynapseIDS, expanding to four pages, one per concern, instead of
    one long scrolling page (issue #178). The plugin stays under Services with
    every other service; only the single page became a submenu.

      Sensors      the capture-instance grid (one synapse-sensor process per
                   interface), add/remove, Apply, per-instance start-stop
      General      master enable, transport posture, bearer token, TLS material,
                   and the shared log level
      Logs         the tail of each instance's sensor.log
      Diagnostics  the on-box selftest (`synapse-sensor doctor`)

    Each child points at OPNsense\SynapseIDSSensor\<page>Controller::indexAction
    (SensorsController, GeneralController, LogsController, DiagnosticsController).
    All four are guarded by the single page-services-synapseidssensor privilege
    in ACL/ACL.xml, whose patterns already glob ui/synapseidssensor/*.
-->
<menu>
    <Services>
        <SynapseIDS VisibleName="SynapseIDS" cssClass="fa fa-shield fa-fw" order="80">
            <Sensors order="10" cssClass="fa fa-microchip fa-fw" url="/ui/synapseidssensor/sensors"/>
            <General order="20" cssClass="fa fa-sliders fa-fw" url="/ui/synapseidssensor/general"/>
            <Logs order="30" cssClass="fa fa-list-alt fa-fw" url="/ui/synapseidssensor/logs"/>
            <Diagnostics order="40" cssClass="fa fa-stethoscope fa-fw" url="/ui/synapseidssensor/diagnostics"/>
        </SynapseIDS>
    </Services>
</menu>
